= Cognitive bias — Technical =

== Normative dependence ==
Let response r be evaluated under benchmark N.

A bias claim requires a systematic relationship:

<pre>
E[r - N] ≠ 0
</pre>

or another structured deviation appropriate to the task.

The benchmark itself can be contested.

== Error decomposition ==
Observed deviation may arise from:

* representation;
* sampling of evidence;
* memory retrieval;
* heuristic substitution;
* motivated search;
* noisy computation;
* response mapping;
* task misunderstanding.

Labeling the output "bias" does not identify the mechanism.

== Ecological rationality ==
Fast-and-frugal approaches ask whether a strategy exploits environmental structure efficiently.

A heuristic can be non-Bayesian or non-optimal under one formal criterion while producing good real-world performance under constraints.

== Replication and task sensitivity ==
Bias effects vary with framing, expertise, incentives, elicitation method, numerical format, and population.

Core claims should distinguish robust phenomenon from proposed mechanism.

